:ruby
  PageHeader = import("/components/PageHeader.haml")
  DocsPage = import("/components/DocsPage.haml")
  DocsSection = import("/components/DocsSection.haml")

%DocsPage
  %PageHeader{
    kicker: "Docs",
    title: "Module Graph And Imports",
    summary: "Klenod collects modules into a graph first, then evaluates Ruby code only when an entry or import value needs it."
  }

  %DocsSection{ title: "Collection Versus Evaluation" }
    :markdown
      Collection reads source, resolves imports, transforms modules, records dependencies, emits assets, stores metadata, and creates a `ModuleRecord`. Evaluation instantiates a `Klenod::Runtime::Mod`, runs transformed Ruby source, and exposes exports.

      `context.entry(...)` and `context.collect(...)` collect without evaluating. `entry.exports`, `entry.call(...)`, `context.exports(...)`, and `context.evaluate(...)` evaluate on demand.

      Build mode depends on this split: it can serialize collected records without running app top-level code.

  %DocsSection{ title: "Module Identifiers" }
    :markdown
      Module ids are source-root-relative by default.

      ```ruby
      import("./Card")
      import("/components/Card")
      import("virtual:router")
      ```

      Relative imports resolve from the importer. Leading slash imports resolve from the configured source directory. Virtual modules use explicit schemes such as `virtual:`.

  %DocsSection{ title: "Eager, Lazy, And Glob Imports" }
    :markdown
      `import("...")` creates an eager dependency. `lazy_import("...")` records a dependency but loads the value only when called.

      ```ruby
      Details = lazy_import("./details")

      def self.render_details
        Details.call::Default.new.render
      end
      ```

      `import_glob("...")` returns a deterministic hash of matched imports. It is eager by default and can be made lazy with `eager: false`.

      ```ruby
      Images = import_glob("./gallery/*.{jpg,png}?width=320&format=webp")
      Pages = import_glob("./pages/*.rb", eager: false)
      ```

      Eager import cycles are errors. Use `lazy_import` for deferred or cyclic branches.
